  "premise_review": [
    "TransportedBaseCaseEuler stores the entire original source : BaseCaseSectionComplex, targetComplex, transport : RodgersTaoDerivedTransport, genuine source/target complex matching equalities and source_euler_matches : transport.eulerTransport.sourceEuler.value = source.euler.value. No field or equality is dropped even when the proof does not use it.",
    "transported_base_case_euler_nonzero is a genuine concrete theorem: it assumes T, obtains the exact supplied targetEuler.value = sourceEuler.value equality, rewrites through the exact source_euler_matches equality, and contradicts T.source.euler_nonzero. Its complete intro/have/apply/rw/exact proof bytes remain unchanged.",
    "The preserved result is only nonzeroness of the supplied integer target Euler value under these exact hypotheses. It constructs no source/target complex, heat family, transport, Euler invariant, nonzero K-theory index or analytic flow action.",
    "Full RodgersTaoEulerTransport and EulerTransport providers were read: the equality used by this proof is the actual euler_eq field of EulerPreservingTransport. Its transport and flow semantic propositions are separate supplied contracts; actual Euler equality is not dismissed as an arbitrary label.",
    "BaseCaseCriticalLinePropagation has an anchor and transportedEuler but no field identifies them. nonzeroIndexToBoundary : Prop has no proof field and is not used by the conclusion theorem; criticalLineConclusion : Prop has its separately supplied witness. The actual theorem simply projects that witness.",
    "Full imported IndexFixedTensorBridge and IndexBoundaryAlignmentBridge sources were read and contain genuine conditional typed implication/existential and boundary conclusion proofs. They are not theorem-free metadata, but this source does not instantiate them or connect them to nonzeroIndexToBoundary/criticalLineConclusion.",
    "Full BaseCaseSectionComplex and BaseCaseIndexAnchor providers were read: actual nonzero value/class evidence coexists with unlinked semantic propositions. No equality/nonzero claim is strengthened into a critical-line statement, K-index interpretation or actual analytic flow result.",
    "New source preserves all original imports, exact theorem terms and record fields, while explicit Folder/Folder.DerivedSheaf opens retain ancestor provider lookup. No imaginary self-provider import, alias, history substitution or proof-body edit is introduced; legacy namespace/provider replay remains unresolved."
  ],
